The files 0018-doc.doc, 0029-doc.doc and 0066-doc.doc come from the DOC-tiny
subset of NapierOne, a mixed-file data set created by the School of Computing
at Edinburgh Napier University in 2021. The subset documentation identifies the
source material as documents recovered from gov.uk websites between January and
March 2021. Original-file URL mapping is held by the data-set researchers and is
available on request; the pinned provenance records the exact source archive,
member path, archive SHA-256, member SHA-256 and CRC-32 instead.

The files 0113-doc.doc, 0670-doc.doc and 0771-doc.doc are additional unchanged
samples from DOC-small.zip in the same dataset. Their individual archive/member
hashes and sizes are pinned in provenance.json.

The files 1825-doc.doc and 4128-doc.doc come from the DOC-total archive of the
same dataset and collection. Their provenance records the archive/member
identity and checksums. 1825-doc.doc contains one EMF and one raster; 4128-doc.doc
contains one EMF and nine rasters. Recompression saves 270,848 and 184,320 bytes
respectively beyond strict CFB compaction, and their LibreOffice page renders
match the originals.

